---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Base
  title={"About · NoCloudware"}
  description={"NoCloudware: independent software by Adrian Goodrich. Licensed once or free, with no subscriptions, monthly fees or pay-per-use."}
  ogImage={"https://www.nocloudware.com/ncw_logo_cloudy.webp"}
  ogType="website"
>
  <div class="legacy-main">
  <div class="container">
    <section style="max-width:750px;margin:0 auto;">
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:2rem;">
        <img src="/ncw_logo_cloudy.webp" alt="NoCloudware" class="product-logo-lg">
      </div>
      <h1>About NoCloudware</h1>
      <div class="mission-text">
        <p>NoCloudware started as a complaint. Software had quietly become rent: a monthly fee that never ends, or a meter that keeps spinning every time you use it. On top of that, most of it only works if you're online, signed in, and trusting somebody else's server with your files.</p>
        <p>The rule that came out of that complaint is simple: <strong>software you own</strong>. Pay once, or don't pay at all. No subscriptions, no freemium traps, no treating your data as the product.</p>
        <p>In practice the rule looks like this. Almost everything here was born from an annoyance of my own, not from a feature roadmap. <strong>TurnAFile</strong> came first: I needed to convert files without depending on the internet, so I built it and didn't depend on the internet either. That's usually how it goes — you hit the problem, you write the thing, and then you wonder why anyone pays a subscription for it.</p>
        <p>The rest are variations on the same theme. <strong>SigilForge</strong> answered a creative need and was given away free. <strong>PoleShift</strong> and <strong>TubeMassDL</strong> were built to do something real without leaning on someone else's cloud or map service. <strong>Bluesk-AI</strong> and <strong>Archivo de Miedos</strong> were experiments in building and sharing something without putting a platform in the middle of it.</p>
        <p>NoCloudware is a small independent studio, run by one person, that keeps to that rule: <strong>minimal, no cloud required, honest about its limits</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2><Icon name="mail" /> Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">For technical support, licensing questions or suggestions: <a href="mailto:nocloudware@outlook.com" style="color:var(--aether-accent);font-weight:600;">nocloudware@outlook.com</a></p>

      <h2><Icon name="money" /> Support the project</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">NoCloudware is an independent project by <strong>Adrian Goodrich</strong>. If you value software without subscriptions, consider supporting its development.</p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <a class="btn btn-donate" href="/donate.html"> Support the project</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

</Base>
